  <prompt>Close the project (FR-17): run `/test-diet` to reconcile tests added/modified during the migration against the ADR-038 build-vs-maintain classifier; run a doc-drift audit; update the `projects/INDEX.md` row (status → complete, last-touched); write the r3 handoff note capturing the net10 baseline assumptions (do NOT re-pin the superseded CVE packages; H1/H2 already fixed; publish-size baseline moved); and file the 6 deferred optional majors (design §6.4) as follow-on issues via `/project-defer-issue-tracking`. This is a MAIN-SESSION-ONLY write task (`.claude/` + `projects/INDEX.md`).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in project close-out, test-diet reconciliation, doc-drift auditing, and cross-project handoffs. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`/test-diet` report exists; doc-drift audit run; `projects/INDEX.md` row updated to complete; the r3 handoff note exists at `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`; the 6 deferred majors are filed as issues via `/project-defer-issue-tracking`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-17 + design §11 (r3 relationship). The r3 handoff is the load-bearing deliverable: r3 re-plans on the net10 baseline and MUST NOT re-pin the CVE packages this project removed, MUST build on the H1/H2 fixes, and MUST note the publish baseline moved. `/test-diet` at project-close is a BINDING gate (root CLAUDE.md §7). The 6 deferred majors (Graph v6/Kiota 2.0, Search v12, AppInsights 3.x, PowerBI v5, Azure.AI.Projects 2.x, Agents.AI GA — plus Http.Polly→Http.Resilience) are logged with concrete reasons (design §4 principle 6: defer nothing silently).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">projects/INDEX.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/r3-handoff.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/test-diet-report.md</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/README.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="061" status="pending">Production cutover complete — the project shipped.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">MAIN-SESSION-ONLY: writes `projects/INDEX.md` + reads/updates `.claude/`-adjacent governance — run in the main session (root §3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">`/test-diet` is a BINDING project-close gate: MAINTAIN-class tests stay at KEEP path, SCAFFOLDING-class deleted; the skill is read-only (emits `git rm`/`git mv` for the reviewer). Cite the report in the wrap-up PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The r3 handoff note MUST state the three baseline assumptions (no re-pin of superseded CVE packages; H1/H2 fixed; publish baseline moved) per design §11.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Project close-out + r3 handoff</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/INDEX.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="r3-relationship" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §11 — the boundary + handoff obligation to code-quality-and-assurance-r3.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-17 + design §11 + ADR-038. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD. Confirm MAIN SESSION.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `/test-diet`; write `notes/test-diet-report.md`; apply the reviewer-approved git rm/mv.</step>
    <step order="2">Run a doc-drift audit over docs/ + `.claude/` for stale net8 references (build commands, runtime strings); fix or log.</step>
    <step order="3">Update `projects/INDEX.md`: flip this project's row to complete + last-touched date.</step>
    <step order="4">Write `notes/r3-handoff.md` with the three baseline assumptions (no re-pin; H1/H2 fixed; publish baseline moved) + any deferred-work pointers.</step>
    <step order="5">File the 6 deferred optional majors as follow-on issues via `/project-defer-issue-tracking`.</step>
    <step order="6">Refresh `README.md` status to complete; update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 090 status to ✅ and mark the project complete.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If `/test-diet` flags AMBIGUOUS tests requiring reviewer judgment, STOP and surface them per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than auto-deleting/keeping — the skill is advisory, the reviewer decides.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">n/a (close-out)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/r3-handoff.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/test-diet-report.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/INDEX.md (row updated)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`/test-diet` report exists and is cited; doc-drift audit run; `projects/INDEX.md` row flipped to complete.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/r3-handoff.md` states the three net10-baseline assumptions for code-quality-and-assurance-r3.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The 6 deferred optional majors are filed as follow-on issues via `/project-defer-issue-tracking`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no MAINTAIN-class test was deleted and no SCAFFOLDING-class test was kept without the reviewer's call.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-17. Main-session-only. Closes the project; r3 is re-planned on the net10 baseline afterward (design §11).</notes>

